WEBVTT

00:02.980 --> 00:05.460
Well, that sure is impressive...

00:13.240 --> 00:17.120
I still get lost occasionally. 
It's just so vast.

00:17.440 --> 00:20.620
Let's head to my study for now.

00:20.620 --> 00:23.260
The sheer scale of this place 
is making me dizzy.

00:23.260 --> 00:26.630
Are there no darker, danker rooms in here?

00:26.630 --> 00:29.010
You're making yourself sound awfully shady.

00:29.010 --> 00:31.460
That'd be because I am legitimately shady.

00:32.000 --> 00:34.090
Saying it with such confidence doesn't help.

00:41.810 --> 00:44.350
Now this is more my speed.

00:44.350 --> 00:48.980
I'm not sure I appreciate my office 
being treated like some shady hideout.

00:49.350 --> 00:53.060
Now, regarding what I hired you for, Zenos...

00:53.060 --> 00:55.310
Something about people 
who've been going missing?

00:55.310 --> 00:56.240
Correct.

00:56.240 --> 00:58.620
Tracking isn't really my thing, y'know.

00:58.620 --> 01:02.660
Don't worry. All I'm asking you to do is go 
around and collect what information you can.

01:02.660 --> 01:07.300
Besides, unlike regular students, 
special research students are able to attend

01:07.300 --> 01:11.090
all manner of programs in the 
Royal Hospital via recommendation.

01:11.090 --> 01:15.220
I imagine being able to look in on a variety 
of programs will make it easier to gather intel.

01:15.220 --> 01:18.090
You're not worried about anyone 
finding out my identity?

01:18.500 --> 01:23.310
You'll be operating as Zeno, 
who has recently returned from abroad.

01:23.310 --> 01:25.270
And you think that'll be enough?

01:25.270 --> 01:28.480
When you have an elite 
healer vouching for you,

01:28.480 --> 01:31.390
security suddenly becomes less of a concern.

01:31.390 --> 01:33.890
Which means if I do screw up somehow,

01:33.890 --> 01:36.990
it'll be your responsibility as 
the person who recommended me.

01:36.990 --> 01:39.350
Our fates are tied together, aren't they?

01:56.050 --> 02:03.560
<b>The Brilliant Healer's
New Life in the Shadows</b>

03:15.920 --> 03:17.710
Welcome back, Zenos!

03:17.710 --> 03:19.590
What're you doing here, Lily?

03:19.590 --> 03:22.270
Dr. Becker signed off on her presence.

03:22.270 --> 03:26.720
Dorm regulations say that significant others 
and family are allowed to cohabitate.

03:27.160 --> 03:29.850
And I'm your wife, Zenos!

03:29.850 --> 03:32.100
No, on paper, you're his little sister.

03:33.850 --> 03:36.480
I'm sure you'll feel more at 
ease with someone you know.

03:36.480 --> 03:39.460
We tried to make this as 
comfortable as possible.

03:39.460 --> 03:43.450
I was worried about leaving her behind, 
so I'm actually pretty grateful.

03:43.880 --> 03:45.150
I'm glad.

03:46.830 --> 03:48.700
Well, I'll see you tomorrow.

03:50.450 --> 03:52.710
Honey!

03:52.710 --> 03:54.330
"Honey"?

03:54.330 --> 03:57.210
Do you want to have something 
to eat? Or have a bath?

03:57.210 --> 03:58.840
Or...

03:58.840 --> 04:00.460
have me?

04:00.460 --> 04:02.280
You heard about the "sister" thing, right?

04:03.340 --> 04:05.590
And who even taught you that?

04:05.590 --> 04:06.850
That would be me.

04:06.850 --> 04:08.720
You're here, too, huh?

04:08.720 --> 04:09.850
Why, exactly?

04:09.850 --> 04:11.040
To be a nuisance.

04:11.040 --> 04:12.600
Yeah, I figured!

04:13.950 --> 04:16.860
Did it even occur to you that, 
with all these healers around,

04:16.860 --> 04:18.860
you'll be exorcised if anyone finds you?

04:20.120 --> 04:22.870
How can I make myself a nuisance 
if I fear that kind of thing?

04:22.870 --> 04:24.950
That's just who you are, huh?

04:24.950 --> 04:29.330
It's not as if there are many capable of 
the kind of healing magic you possess.

04:29.330 --> 04:30.380
Did you say something?

04:30.380 --> 04:32.080
Not a thing.

04:32.080 --> 04:33.330
"And thus,

04:33.330 --> 04:36.050
a minor request from the Royal Hospital

04:36.050 --> 04:40.800
ultimately ended up turning 
into a major incident!"

04:40.800 --> 04:44.090
Do you have to make a scary-sounding 
prophecy the second you show up?

04:47.590 --> 04:51.470
So, Zenos... or rather, Zeno.

04:51.470 --> 04:53.840
How did orientation go?

04:53.840 --> 04:56.200
Looks like I'm going to be 
running all over the place,

04:56.200 --> 05:02.080
but I don't even know how to 
get a normal healer's license.

05:02.080 --> 05:03.940
Well, let's see...

05:03.940 --> 05:07.480
First, one applies to take the exam 
to attend a healer preparatory school,

05:07.480 --> 05:10.580
and if you pass, you spend 
a few years learning there.

05:10.580 --> 05:15.210
Afterward, if you pass the healer 
exam, you earn your license.

05:15.210 --> 05:17.470
That sounds like a ton of investment.

05:17.470 --> 05:19.710
Man, healers are kind of impressive.

05:19.710 --> 05:22.290
Coming from you, that is...
certainly a statement.

05:25.090 --> 05:28.880
After that, you may be assigned 
to a branch of the Royal Hospital,

05:28.880 --> 05:31.330
or earn an adventuring license 
to work in the field.

05:31.330 --> 05:35.100
Some people also work directly for 
the aristocracy or join the military.

05:35.100 --> 05:37.650
Of course, once you're working and 
have made a name for yourself,

05:37.650 --> 05:40.560
you have the option of getting 
examined and going up in rank.

05:41.520 --> 05:44.440
An exam to go up in rank?

05:44.440 --> 05:47.540
And this place is where 
that stuff is handled, huh?

05:47.540 --> 05:50.400
Correct. Most of the students 
are people here to either

05:50.400 --> 05:52.330
do research or advance their education,

05:52.330 --> 05:54.580
people interested in more advanced healing,

05:54.580 --> 05:58.330
or staff and administration.

05:58.330 --> 06:00.910
I'm starting to get a headache.

06:00.910 --> 06:04.130
For now, why don't you tell me 
more about our missing people?

06:04.130 --> 06:05.460
Sure.

06:05.460 --> 06:08.970
His name is Afread, and he's 
an upperclassman of mine.

06:08.970 --> 06:13.350
He's an advanced healer and the 
deputy head of the laboratory.

06:13.350 --> 06:17.600
He's incredibly talented and kind, 
as well as considerate.

06:17.600 --> 06:24.570
Dr. Becker even said that Afread was a major 
contributor in creating the cure for Red Lung.

06:25.780 --> 06:28.950
Sounds like someone 
who's worth finding, then.

06:28.950 --> 06:30.990
Do you have any leads?

06:30.990 --> 06:33.230
There is one thing, but...

06:35.230 --> 06:36.330
Who's that?

06:36.330 --> 06:38.460
Professor Goldran.

06:38.460 --> 06:40.830
He's the vice director 
of the Royal Hospital,

06:40.830 --> 06:43.710
and a class seven advanced healer.

06:43.710 --> 06:45.340
Class seven?

06:45.340 --> 06:46.620
Yes.

06:46.620 --> 06:49.510
Each healing level—beginner, 
intermediate, and advanced—

06:49.510 --> 06:52.050
is further split into seven classes.

06:52.050 --> 06:57.850
A class seven advanced healer is as high as 
one gets without becoming an elite healer.

06:57.850 --> 06:59.550
Huh...

06:59.550 --> 07:02.810
Well, he's got a huge entourage.
 Must be a big deal.

07:02.810 --> 07:06.070
He's in the running to be the 
next director, after all.

07:06.070 --> 07:09.840
The current director takes a lot of 
time off due to his advanced age,

07:09.840 --> 07:13.570
so it's fair to say that the vice director 
has the most authority at the moment.

07:13.570 --> 07:19.200
And the Royal Hospital has changed 
a bit since he became vice director.

07:19.200 --> 07:22.140
While the wealthy receive enthusiastic care,

07:22.140 --> 07:26.570
there's been increasingly less attention 
paid to the other patients.

07:26.570 --> 07:29.930
Professor Goldran seems more interested 
in advancing his political agenda

07:29.930 --> 07:32.470
than improving his healing abilities.

07:32.470 --> 07:35.250
There are even rumors that 
his class seven promotion

07:35.250 --> 07:39.640
came from making good use of support 
he's received from some major nobles.

07:40.160 --> 07:42.850
Better to stay clear of him, then.

07:42.850 --> 07:47.440
I'm afraid that's not an 
option for you, Zeno.

07:48.440 --> 07:52.950
There's a chance he might be 
involved in Afread's disappearance.

07:53.270 --> 07:55.740
Being so ambitious, Professor 
Goldran seems to want to

07:55.740 --> 07:59.410
gather as many talented individuals 
beneath him as possible.

07:59.410 --> 08:02.960
He had called on Afread, on the 
pretext of a loan from our lab.

08:02.960 --> 08:04.830
And Becker was fine with that?

08:04.830 --> 08:09.800
The professor had contributed financially 
to the manufacturing of the Red Lung cure,

08:09.800 --> 08:12.400
so the doctor felt indebted.

08:12.400 --> 08:17.600
Plus, Afread himself thought it wouldn't 
be bad to expand his horizons.

08:17.600 --> 08:22.140
But a month later, he went missing.

08:22.140 --> 08:23.600
What did Goldran have to say?

08:23.600 --> 08:27.940
He insists that he has no idea what happened 
and is actually inconvenienced by it.

08:27.940 --> 08:30.230
I get what you're trying to tell me.

08:30.230 --> 08:32.070
But how do I approach him?

08:32.330 --> 08:33.500
That won't be a problem.

08:33.500 --> 08:37.610
As you distinguish yourself in the assorted 
programs, he'll probably contact you.

08:37.610 --> 08:39.330
You make that sound so easy.

08:39.330 --> 08:42.020
I have a hard time imagining a 
healer from a run-down clinic

08:42.020 --> 08:44.230
distinguishing himself in the Royal Hospital.

08:44.960 --> 08:47.580
Wait... Zeno, do you not realize—

08:47.580 --> 08:48.960
Hey, Umin!

08:49.850 --> 08:52.490
What're you doing, sitting 
off to the side like this?

08:52.490 --> 08:53.970
Cresson...

08:53.970 --> 08:56.140
I'm allowed to eat wherever I want, aren't I?

08:56.140 --> 08:58.470
Whoa, simmer down, now.

08:58.470 --> 09:03.480
We of the Goldran faction appreciate 
you making plenty of room for us.

09:08.690 --> 09:10.680
You're the special research student, right?

09:11.320 --> 09:16.820
Do your best not to embarrass 
your sponsor, you hear?

09:17.220 --> 09:18.440
What's his deal?

09:18.440 --> 09:20.240
Don't worry about him.

09:20.240 --> 09:25.080
We're classmates, but ever since he was scouted 
by Goldran's group, he's gotten a big head.

09:25.080 --> 09:26.650
Uh-huh...

09:26.650 --> 09:29.000
Well, for now, I'm heading to class.

09:32.060 --> 09:33.210
<i>The structure of the epidermis...</i>

09:33.640 --> 09:34.840
<i>The distribution of muscle...</i>

09:35.360 --> 09:36.970
<i>The layout of blood vessels and nerves...</i>

09:37.480 --> 09:38.840
<i>The positioning of organs...</i>

09:40.840 --> 09:42.150
<i>Today's the day I pull this off.</i>

09:45.770 --> 09:47.760
What's the big deal, old timer?!

09:47.760 --> 09:49.980
Don't use that power on the dead.

09:49.980 --> 09:52.160
It should be saved for the living.

10:01.070 --> 10:03.990
You've both improved a 
lot over this past year.

10:03.990 --> 10:06.250
Looks like I was right about you.

10:06.250 --> 10:09.120
I'm the one who brought Veritra in, though.

10:09.120 --> 10:14.460
And I don't want you two getting cocky 
just because you can fix a few wounds.

10:14.460 --> 10:17.860
Being able to heal wounds only 
makes a healer third-rate.

10:17.860 --> 10:19.130
Right, Master.

10:19.500 --> 10:21.720
A healer is second-rate if they 
can wholly heal a person...

10:21.720 --> 10:24.850
And only first-rate if they can 
make the world a better place.

10:24.850 --> 10:27.980
Trust me, I remember. I've heard it so many 
times, people have said it to me in my dreams.

10:28.790 --> 10:30.100
Really?

10:30.100 --> 10:32.020
Well, as long as you get it.

10:35.600 --> 10:38.100
We'll now begin the lecture.

10:38.740 --> 10:41.790
I specialize in adventurer-adjacent healing.

10:41.790 --> 10:43.710
Today's topic is the undead.

10:43.710 --> 10:48.250
I'll introduce you to the latest findings on 
these monsters that roam the world after death.

10:48.880 --> 10:50.500
<i>Huh...</i>

10:50.500 --> 10:51.930
<i>Pretty interesting.</i>

10:52.500 --> 10:55.590
<i>A lot of it I know from 
when I was adventuring,</i>

10:55.590 --> 10:58.880
<i>but the systematic way it's 
organized makes it easy to absorb.</i>

10:59.650 --> 11:01.820
Does anyone have any questions?

11:02.480 --> 11:04.630
Are we going to discuss wraiths at all?

11:04.630 --> 11:06.000
A good question,

11:06.000 --> 11:11.850
but we don't know that much about the 
highest-ranked among undead monsters.

11:11.850 --> 11:13.440
And that's for two reasons.

11:13.440 --> 11:16.020
One is that there aren't 
many eyewitness reports.

11:16.020 --> 11:20.740
The other is that most parties who 
have challenged them were wiped out.

11:20.740 --> 11:25.620
The most pertinent thing is that if you 
encounter a wraith, the best thing to do is run.

11:25.620 --> 11:28.950
The ones that can speak are 
particularly dangerous.

11:28.950 --> 11:32.120
In general, if a monster is verbal, 
you know it's incredibly powerful.

11:32.120 --> 11:35.000
And when a wraith is verbal, 
it's more than just about anyone can handle.

11:35.290 --> 11:37.380
Wait, seriously?

11:37.670 --> 11:40.720
<i>I've got a talking wraith kicking 
back in my room right now...</i>

11:40.720 --> 11:42.900
<i>I probably shouldn't mention that.</i>

11:44.010 --> 11:48.390
As we wrap up, have any among 
you fought the undead before?

11:48.390 --> 11:51.350
If you have, I'd like you to share 
your experience with the others.

11:54.380 --> 11:58.320
My name is Cresson Wembley, and I'm 
a member of the Goldran Laboratory.

11:58.320 --> 12:04.190
I was an adventurer for a few years, 
and have taken down around 30 ghosts.

12:08.440 --> 12:12.000
How about you, special research student?

12:12.000 --> 12:12.840
Huh?

12:15.500 --> 12:18.130
<i>I need to make a name for myself,</i>

12:18.130 --> 12:20.060
<i>but standing out too much is a bad idea.</i>

12:20.060 --> 12:22.590
<i>I can probably take out 50 at once, but...</i>

12:22.590 --> 12:24.970
<i>Might be smarter to just match his story.</i>

12:25.350 --> 12:27.970
Uh, I'm at around 30, too.

12:29.150 --> 12:30.720
Don't lie, man.

12:30.720 --> 12:34.850
I'm not. Really, 30 is about 
the most I can beat at once.

12:34.850 --> 12:39.110
Seriously, you don't need to... Wait, "at once"?

12:39.110 --> 12:42.140
Wait, you didn't mean 30 at once?

12:42.140 --> 12:45.890
You're Zeno, the special 
research student, correct?

12:45.890 --> 12:48.370
Could you explain what you mean?

12:48.650 --> 12:50.270
There's not much to explain.

12:50.270 --> 12:53.540
If you go to the underground labyrinth, 
that place is crawling with ghosts,

12:53.540 --> 12:57.250
and the best way to deal with them is to 
cast Heal on as many as you can at once.

12:57.250 --> 13:01.210
The underground labyrinth... 
of Garminton, you mean?!

13:01.210 --> 13:04.590
I think that's what the name was, yeah.

13:04.590 --> 13:10.350
Zeno. Even gold-class parties 
hesitate to set foot in that place.

13:13.480 --> 13:15.350
<i>What the hell is his deal?</i>

13:15.350 --> 13:17.350
<i>There's no way that was true.</i>

13:17.850 --> 13:19.520
<i>I don't like him.</i>

13:25.280 --> 13:27.430
You said your name was Zeno, right?

13:27.430 --> 13:30.480
Don't just spout nonsense 
because you want to stand out.

13:30.480 --> 13:33.260
I'm actually trying to avoid 
standing out, to be honest.

13:33.870 --> 13:37.330
We'll now begin our lecture 
on healing magic circles.

13:37.870 --> 13:41.210
<i>If I'm being honest, I don't 
understand magic circles.</i>

13:41.210 --> 13:43.840
<i>If I have time to spend 
drawing that kind of thing,</i>

13:43.840 --> 13:47.050
<i>I figure it's faster to just heal my patient.</i>

13:48.220 --> 13:52.720
Now, if one of you would come up here 
and draw your best magic circle.

13:54.100 --> 13:56.100
Allow me, sir.

14:01.000 --> 14:02.980
It looks pretty good.

14:02.980 --> 14:06.140
I don't suppose you'd like 
to join my laboratory?

14:06.140 --> 14:10.240
Oh, no, I already work for Professor Goldran.

14:11.370 --> 14:15.620
Professor, I believe the special research 
student would like to show what he can do.

14:18.790 --> 14:22.250
<i>My teacher showed me one 
magic circle a long time ago.</i>

14:22.250 --> 14:25.510
<i>That's the only one I know, 
so I guess that's what I'm drawing.</i>

14:27.340 --> 14:30.220
I've never seen a magic 
circle that looks like that.

14:30.220 --> 14:34.220
Looks like the gold plating's come off the 
big-talking special research student already!

14:34.850 --> 14:36.600
Th-This magic circle...

14:36.990 --> 14:38.720
This goes beyond simple healing magic.

14:38.720 --> 14:42.860
The cardinal directions are 
marked by infinite spirals...

14:42.860 --> 14:44.720
Is this for regeneration?

14:44.720 --> 14:46.810
But something's still different...

14:46.810 --> 14:50.940
Oh, that's actually it, 
but it's a real weird one.

14:50.940 --> 14:55.140
Like, if the patient's lost multiple fingers, 
it'll randomly grow one back.

14:55.140 --> 14:56.870
S-Say what?!

14:56.870 --> 14:59.260
Conditional branching and random sampling?

14:59.260 --> 15:02.130
I had no idea you could cram that 
much into a single magic circle!

15:02.130 --> 15:04.890
But this would require a 
massive amount of mana.

15:04.890 --> 15:06.500
Surely no human could activate it.

15:06.500 --> 15:07.960
I can, though.

15:10.040 --> 15:12.110
It's honestly not that useful.

15:12.110 --> 15:14.970
Regenerating a finger 
with magic is way faster.

15:15.970 --> 15:18.220
I have no idea what you're 
saying, and I don't care.

15:18.220 --> 15:22.350
More than anything, I want 
you to join my laboratory!

15:22.350 --> 15:24.610
Uh, no, I kinda have stuff to take care of...

15:25.860 --> 15:29.620
<i>What is this? What the hell is he?!</i>

15:31.590 --> 15:34.370
There's something I think 
you should know, Professor.

15:34.650 --> 15:36.020
What is it?

15:36.020 --> 15:39.370
There are rumors of an interesting 
individual in the school.

15:39.370 --> 15:43.380
A healer capable of defeating 
30 ghosts at once.

15:43.380 --> 15:46.950
His name is Zeno, and he's this 
year's special research student.

15:46.950 --> 15:49.460
A special research student?

15:49.990 --> 15:53.440
Do you believe our faction is so 
insignificant that some random

15:53.440 --> 15:55.600
special research student 
should be allowed to join?

15:55.600 --> 15:57.100
My apologies, sir!

15:57.100 --> 15:58.680
Pardon me, Professor.

15:58.680 --> 16:03.230
I have a report. There are multiple 
reports of undead at the Suula graveyard.

16:03.660 --> 16:05.980
Assign someone to deal with the matter.

16:06.590 --> 16:11.600
In fact, send the special research student 
who can take out 30 ghosts in one blow.

16:11.600 --> 16:13.860
If he proves to live up to his claims,

16:13.860 --> 16:16.980
we may just have a spot for him.

16:16.980 --> 16:18.100
Very good, sir.

16:20.110 --> 16:22.750
You're going to fight some undead, Zenos?

16:22.750 --> 16:24.060
Yeah.

16:24.060 --> 16:26.130
Exorcising the undead, eh?

16:26.130 --> 16:27.880
That certainly means trouble.

16:27.880 --> 16:28.960
Tell me about it.

16:28.960 --> 16:31.340
I meant for the undead.

16:31.720 --> 16:36.820
If a bunch have shown up... Undead really 
do tend to gather at graveyards, huh?

16:36.820 --> 16:41.100
Since the church oversees this one, 
this kind of thing is rare, apparently.

16:41.100 --> 16:42.960
They're not sure what caused it.

16:44.350 --> 16:46.100
Go on, enjoy your meal.

16:46.100 --> 16:48.470
You weren't the one who made it. It was Lily.

16:48.470 --> 16:50.150
Are you going to eat, Carmilla?

16:50.150 --> 16:52.740
I'll take extra chicken, if you don't mind.

16:52.740 --> 16:55.410
And if you give me any carrots, 
I'll curse you and your descendants.

16:55.410 --> 16:57.490
You have no trouble eating solid matter?

16:58.850 --> 17:01.490
All things are possible with enough spirit!

17:01.490 --> 17:04.320
I get the feeling if I just wrote 
down my observations on you,

17:04.320 --> 17:06.750
it'd be enough to earn me a degree.

17:12.460 --> 17:14.090
Ch-Charge!

17:14.090 --> 17:16.220
Follow me!

17:16.220 --> 17:19.780
Root of all life, by your 
blessing, grant amelioration.

17:19.780 --> 17:20.970
Heal!

17:23.910 --> 17:26.680
They're being pretty thorough, 
only taking out one or two at a time.

17:26.680 --> 17:28.610
It seems kinda inefficient, though.

17:28.610 --> 17:31.860
I can only imagine it'd 
seem that way to you.

17:31.860 --> 17:34.240
Damn it! We can't keep up with these numbers!

17:34.240 --> 17:35.360
It's no good!

17:37.940 --> 17:39.240
High Heal.

17:43.120 --> 17:44.310
That was great.

17:44.310 --> 17:47.750
They were all gathered in one spot.
That made it easier to deal with them.

17:47.750 --> 17:49.850
<i>I didn't quite expect... this.</i>

17:51.710 --> 17:56.090
Did you see that?! This is what Cresson 
of the Goldran faction is capable of!

17:56.090 --> 17:57.630
Was that you, Cresson?

17:57.630 --> 17:59.590
That was some amazing healing magic.

17:59.590 --> 18:01.720
No, Zeno was the one who...

18:01.720 --> 18:06.100
Huh? As if a special research student 
could be capable of something like that!

18:06.100 --> 18:10.520
Go on, report our success and my 
contribution to your teachers!

18:10.520 --> 18:11.600
You're dismissed!

18:11.600 --> 18:13.230
Cresson, wait!

18:14.410 --> 18:17.610
Listen up! There's no way I accept you!

18:17.880 --> 18:19.110
Okay.

18:19.110 --> 18:21.620
What the hell is your deal?!

18:21.620 --> 18:26.250
Why'd they make me observe this special research 
student freak who showed up out of nowhere?

18:26.250 --> 18:27.280
Observe?

18:27.880 --> 18:30.270
Forget it! I'm done!

18:33.130 --> 18:35.670
The undead aren't dealt with yet, though.

18:36.340 --> 18:39.090
What do you mean?

18:40.160 --> 18:40.970
It's coming.

18:50.850 --> 18:52.890
A zombie... king?

18:52.890 --> 18:55.700
Why is such a dangerous 
monster suddenly popping up?!

18:55.700 --> 18:58.040
Cresson! You're our only hope!

18:58.040 --> 19:00.960
Use some incredible healing 
magic to slow it down!

19:00.960 --> 19:02.740
S-Sure...

19:02.740 --> 19:05.990
They seem to have high expectations for you,

19:05.990 --> 19:08.250
Cresson of the Goldran faction.

19:08.250 --> 19:11.650
Umin, you jerk! We're classmates, 
and you're not gonna help?!

19:11.650 --> 19:14.880
What? You need help from the likes of me?

19:14.880 --> 19:17.520
You, Cresson of the Goldran faction?

19:18.210 --> 19:20.340
Yeah, I know.

19:20.340 --> 19:22.860
You don't want me interfering, right?

19:23.850 --> 19:26.850
Oh... well... glad you get it.

19:26.850 --> 19:28.980
Hurry up and call for reinforcements!

19:28.980 --> 19:32.100
I'll hold it off until then...

19:33.380 --> 19:36.610
H-Here I come! Say your prayers!

19:37.600 --> 19:40.640
Pretty bold of him, 
but why's his voice cracking?

19:40.640 --> 19:43.870
It's almost a textbook example 
of getting what you deserve.

19:43.870 --> 19:50.120
Light of life that dwells deep within, hear my 
prayers, and let your blessing shine forth here!

19:51.640 --> 19:53.860
High Heal!

19:58.100 --> 20:00.210
That was my best magic, and it...

20:09.600 --> 20:11.170
You see that, peanut gallery?!

20:11.170 --> 20:12.340
We're evenly matched...

20:12.340 --> 20:15.040
No, I managed to strike 
first, so I have the edge!

20:15.040 --> 20:17.730
It didn't lay a finger on me!

20:19.560 --> 20:22.490
I suppose this explains why 
so many have been appearing.

20:22.490 --> 20:25.780
Undead are drawn to more powerful undead.

20:25.780 --> 20:28.120
This zombie king must be the root of all this.

20:28.120 --> 20:29.770
The zombie king...

20:30.440 --> 20:32.460
Something seems off about that.

20:32.460 --> 20:37.130
I also wonder why he's not 
using healing magic anymore.

20:37.130 --> 20:39.090
Well, he was lying before.

20:39.090 --> 20:40.960
Wait, he was?

20:40.960 --> 20:41.970
Yes.

20:41.970 --> 20:44.690
But I'd rather you didn't help him.

20:44.690 --> 20:47.440
He's earned a bit of pain 
for his shenanigans.

20:47.440 --> 20:50.590
You say that, but I can tell 
you're worried about him.

20:50.590 --> 20:53.140
Wh-What makes you say that?!

20:53.140 --> 20:56.440
The fact that you stuck 
around kinda suggests it.

20:56.440 --> 21:00.610
W-Well, someone should collect his remains...

21:00.950 --> 21:02.860
W-We are classmates, after all.

21:04.860 --> 21:08.300
But he's just been rolling around 
instead of fighting, hasn't he?

21:11.830 --> 21:16.620
Root of all life, by your 
blessing, grant amelioration...

21:16.620 --> 21:17.500
Heal.

21:24.500 --> 21:26.090
L-Let me go!

21:26.970 --> 21:28.090
Cresson!

21:29.220 --> 21:31.350
H-Help!

21:39.360 --> 21:40.610
Mega Heal!

21:54.400 --> 21:56.560
Wh-Who asked you to help me?

21:56.560 --> 21:58.620
Well, you did. Quite loudly.

21:58.620 --> 22:01.130
You were bawling, going, "Help!"

22:01.130 --> 22:02.960
Kn-Knock it off! I was not!

22:02.960 --> 22:06.480
No, I heard it quite clearly.

22:04.000 --> 22:06.480
<i>Drawn to more powerful undead...</i>

22:06.480 --> 22:08.570
I would've done just fine without your help!

22:08.030 --> 22:10.520
Look, uh... Sorry.

22:08.570 --> 22:10.520
If you hadn't gotten so full of yourself—

22:13.740 --> 22:16.730
Are you okay, Carmilla? Are you sick?

22:18.170 --> 22:23.800
Quite the jest, suggesting that the greatest 
of the undead such as myself could get sick.

23:55.530 --> 24:00.000
Faction Infiltration

23:57.270 --> 23:58.790
"Faction Infiltration."
